Building a HeaderMap from an iterator with a very large number of repeated header names causes a panic instead of succeeding. For example:

```rust
let name = HeaderName::from_static("h");
let value = HeaderValue::from_static("0");
let pairs: Vec<_> = std::iter::repeat((name, value)).take(24_577).collect();
let map = HeaderMap::from_iter(pairs);
```

This panics (likely a capacity/overflow panic) even though inserting the same values one at a time works fine. Extending a HeaderMap should never panic just because the iterator's size hint exceeds what the map's internal table can index. Please fix this so building a HeaderMap from an iterator with many values under a single header name succeeds without panicking.
